WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.310
That's top-class Koshihikari!

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:09.950
And this is "Love at First Sight,"

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.530
and that one is Milky Queen!

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:27.080
Don-don-don! Delicious 
rice! Don-don-don!

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.630
Don-don-don! Rice! Rice! Don-don-don!

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.820
Eat it! Eat up! Don-don-don!

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:39.660
Rule the land! Eat rice 
and you'll rule the land!

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.910
A powerful person! 
The ruler of the land!

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:46.020
Hideyoshi is the ruler of the land!

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.020
Aww, jeez, guys...

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:54.030
Hideyoshi! Hideyoshi! Hideyoshi!

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:54.030
Hideyoshi... Hideyoshi!

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.440
Hideyoshi!

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:57.420
Hideyoshi!

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:02.040
Put me down guys, 
I can't eat the rice...

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.950
I said Hideyoshi!

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.000
Huh?

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.880
You had another dream about rice?

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.220
Yeah, I just ate and ate 
and couldn't get enough.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.370
You always eat so much, though.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:49.310
Aww, I'm embarrassed.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.730
Since I'm a guest at your house, 
I'm actually holding back.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.990
I dunno whether to be impressed

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:57.520
or annoyed that you call 
that "holding back."

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:01.290
Well, I love rice more 
than anyone in Japan!

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:03.030
That's a weird thing to be proud of.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.370
What'll you do if we can't
get much rice in the village?

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:09.420
That'd be terrible if 
there was a bad harvest!

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.110
Even in your world, you used 
to have bad harvests...

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:14.250
it must've been terrible.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.280
I guess so, yeah. 
I heard once from my grandma...

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.880
See that rock up there?

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.220
It's called the Mountain 
Woman's Tea Table.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.940
She said girls used to dance up there.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:24.980
Dance?

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:25.600
Why?

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:28.770
If a girl offers a dance 
to the gods up there,

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.700
it guarantees a good harvest.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:33.150
Only if she makes it back alive, though.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.650
Makes it back alive? 
What does that mean?

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.360
It's an old folk tale around here.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:44.200
In exchange for a good 
harvest, the gods took the

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:48.040
girls who danced and didn't bring them back.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.120
That sounds interesting.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:55.790
Hey, you better not be thinking about doing it!

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.830
I won't, I won't.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.840
But it means we would get lots of rice, right?

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.590
I said no!

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:04.130
I know!

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.730
Nothing happened.

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.740
Well, it is just a story.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.220
Even if nothing happens, 
if I can make myself believe

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.660
there'll be a good harvest, 
it'll be totally worth it.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:32.000
Now then, let's eat.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.340
The moon comes out in this world, too.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:40.090
Which means I can have an elegant 
meal by the light of the moon!

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.590
Hey! Wait! Hey!

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.360
Hey, wait!

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.940
Catch!

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:19.470
What is this place?

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.590
Two doors.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:28.390
Which means this leads somewhere.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:33.970
Okay, so I can get out this way.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:36.480
And what's on the other side?

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:42.060
What a lovely morning.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:46.380
But I can't survive 
unless I eat breakfast.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:48.450
All living things must...

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:52.990
Well, it doesn't have to be 
breakfast, but they must eat.

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:58.500
I'm crying...

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.080
What are these tears?

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.790
Tears of gratitude or sadness?

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.790
Either way, I will eat the white rice.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.550
Oh, so this is a dream!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:14.010
Wait, if it's a dream, 
I can leave whenever.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:17.100
Which means... I'm going 
this way instead.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.410
It seems kinda fun.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.660
Hi there, Mr. Rice!

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.580
Congratulations!

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:30.800
You are our 10,000th customer!

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.650
Congratulations!

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:33.740
What's going on here?

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:37.180
Well, you're our 10,000th customer.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.860
We have a welcome meal prepared.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:42.280
Please, enjoy yourself.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:45.130
I-I can eat all this?

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:48.670
Yes. You're our first customer in ages, and our 10,00th one at that.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.970
We must do something to celebrate.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.340
Now eat up.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:54.850
Thank you for coming!

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:58.840
Man, dreams always have the best stuff!

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:00.240
All right, then.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.020
Wait a second, monkey-girl.

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:06.100
That's a dream for you.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:07.760
You get interrupted at the worst times.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.650
And it's the boss.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:11.990
I can't disobey the boss.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.320
What are you talking about?

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.710
This isn't your dream.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:20.050
Of course it is, Boss!

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:22.830
This stuff can't be real.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:25.120
What are you talking about?

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.530
I'm real.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:30.480
Well sure, but so am I.

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.590
And this is my dream.

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:35.360
So I'm just part of your dream?

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:38.450
I was after your secret 
treasure and I ended up here.

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:41.230
So I can't be part of your dream.

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:44.170
So does that mean I'm part of yours?

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:45.350
That's right.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:47.980
'Cause this can't be real, right?

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:52.140
Sure. But is it possible 
for one of us to be just

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:54.390
part of the other's dream?

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:57.030
Let's see if this really is a dream.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:58.200
Here.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.870
Hey, stop!

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:06.790
See, you're the dream.

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:08.570
You stupid monkey!

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:13.300
If I'm also in the dream,
anything can happen to me, too!

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.810
See, you're a dream, too!

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:21.180
You got me there...

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.190
But if this is your dream

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.310
then I'm part of your dream, too, aren't I?

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:28.040
Isn't that kind of sad?

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:30.590
Sad?

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:33.220
'Cause that means you're all alone

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:34.720
and just thinking of what I'm saying.

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:36.990
That's sad, isn't it?

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:41.790
Then isn't it sad that you're 
claiming this is your dream?

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:42.970
It is.

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:47.110
In other words, it's better 
not to think of it at all.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:50.640
You were the first one to 
say I was a dream, Boss.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:53.280
Don't worry about the little things.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.820
Well, just sit down and eat something.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:57.790
Of course, you don't 
have to tell me twice!

00:08:57.790 --> 00:08:59.760
This is a feast.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.260
A feast? It's all rice.

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:04.790
This is a feast to me.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.810
We'll start with some tarako...

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:08.230
One second.

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:10.960
Another interruption!

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:14.140
You're our 10,000th rice-loving customer.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:15.980
We'd like to test you.

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:20.660
It's possible that you are 
the hero who will save us.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:21.540
Hero?

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.620
Yes. There is a legend.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:26.370
That when we are in danger,

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:31.340
the girl who knows us best 
will appear and save us.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:36.630
So we want to test to see if you're 
the girl who knows us best.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.140
Test me? How?

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:42.970
Please tell us, which one
 is actually Akitakomachi rice.

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:46.860
How can you tell like that?

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:48.520
And we've never even 
seen you before!

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.770
That doesn't matter.

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:56.270
No, as you can see, we're all different.

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:57.280
You're the same!

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.390
Oh my, are your eyes bad?

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:00.380
Perhaps her ears?

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:02.660
No, I think it's her head.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:06.750
Okay, rice, line up! 
I'm gonna chop you in half!

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.670
No, Boss!

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:14.050
So the girl who was staying 
at Noriko's has gone missing?

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:17.630
Yesterday, I told her about the 
Mountain Woman's Tea Table,

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:20.110
so I thought she went there...

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:22.050
But we couldn't find her.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:25.060
There were traces of her 
having been there, but...

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:28.180
Very bad. This is very bad.

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:30.380
What do you mean, Grandma?

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:34.730
That ceremony sends girls to another world.

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:37.940
It's in exchange for the bountiful harvest.

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:40.740
But we don't need it anymore.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.490
Then Hideyoshi-chan...

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:45.580
She'll probably never come back!

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:46.720
No!

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:49.620
However, some have.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:51.180
How?

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:54.310
It's up to the girls.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:58.510
The problem is how much they love rice.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:03.170
How much they want the 
harvest to be good.

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:07.150
Girls these days are never hungry.

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:08.920
So I don't think it's possible.

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:11.560
But Hideyoshi isn't a normal girl.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:17.820
Come on, Boss... 
It's rice, getting mad won't help.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:21.570
If it's rice, then there's no problem 
with cutting it right now.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:23.820
Actually, why is there talking 
rice in the first place?

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:26.200
That's the real question.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:29.550
No, rice have souls.

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:31.960
You're smart, Boss.
You should know that.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.080
What are you...

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:37.050
The farmers worked hard to raise it.

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:39.530
It has to have a soul.

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:42.550
You're smart, Boss.
You should know that.

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:47.870
When you're as smart as I am,

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:50.500
you don't even need to think about it!

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:51.750
You're so smart, Boss!

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:53.880
You came up with all 
those brilliant plans!

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:57.770
You should know how to 
find the answer already.

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:58.630
Right?

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:00.810
Well... yeah.

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:03.950
Fortunately, I know 
what you're thinking.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:07.650
So if you leave it to 
me, I'll just go do it.

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:11.730
Oh... okay, it's up to 
you then, monkey girl.

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:14.080
Okay! Time to get started.

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:21.970
Akitakomachi!

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:24.770
She's right!

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:29.210
I knew it, too.

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:30.720
I knew it was that one.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:35.850
You picked the right one. 
You are our savior.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:39.530
Now take this item of the savior.

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:41.240
Zori sandals?

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:43.660
What are these guys thinking?

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:57.980
Hey, wait!

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:00.250
Hey, what am I supposed 
to do with these?

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:08.730
They told me to save them,

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:11.340
but the people I'm supposed 
to save are gone.

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:25.450
I guess our only choice is to walk.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:27.700
We're surrounded by rice fields...

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.210
Somebody's up ahead.

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.950
We finally met someone?

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:33.120
Hey, it's a scarecrow.

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:35.290
I'm a scarecrow.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:36.870
It talked!

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.250
It sure did.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:41.300
I can offer you entertainment 
besides talking.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.070
Have a look.

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:50.810
Look inside the box for fun!

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:54.010
A wonderful theater of hope and dreams!

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:56.480
Look inside, look inside the box!

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:58.580
Uh, what should we do?

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:01.440
I guess... we look inside the box.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:09.630
I need food.

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:11.450
You'll find it someday.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:18.560
If the past is not 
included in the future,

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:20.630
then atonement itself is a futile act.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.790
Not what we're talking about.

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:26.460
As long as there are eyes that watch,

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:28.780
this place cannot be purgatory.

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:32.570
Without eyes, we are merely costumes.

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:34.270
I'd like to wear a costume.

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:36.240
I can't count on eyes.

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:41.950
Then how shall we pray for atonement?

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:45.290
It is possible to pray for nothing.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:48.040
But your prayers will 
disappear into the void.

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:51.280
Then whose hands are they that pray?

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:54.030
If nothing else, you have no hands.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:58.450
Hey, um... What is this?

00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:01.750
What is it? It's a play, of course.

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:05.130
Don't plays have to be 
something you understand?

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:09.550
Some plays aren't meant to be understood.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:12.440
There are two types of plays 
you don't understand.

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:15.100
Those written so you 
will not understand.

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:16.810
And those with no content.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:18.060
Then which is this?

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:20.980
There's no such thing as a 
play with content.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.310
Don't say things that don't make sense.

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:26.800
The real world is made of plays.

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:29.530
It is unthinkable for
them to have content.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:33.280
And some people are sad, 
and cry because of this.

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:35.700
If you cannot heal their sorrow,

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.240
you cannot call yourself a savior.

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.850
A savior?

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:41.090
Yes, a savior.

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:45.290
Here, consoling those in sorrow 
is their only salvation.

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.750
And what happens then?

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:49.510
If nothing else, 
you'll be called a savior.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.890
Not sure what's going on here,

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:55.070
but it's pretty clear we 
want nothing to do with it.

00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:56.760
Let's get going.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.270
Rikyuu!

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:05.480
Welcome.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:06.690
Where are we?

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:09.740
A difficult question to answer.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:11.060
What are you talking about?

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:12.990
Of course it's an easy 
question to answer.

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:14.130
Now, now, Boss.

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:15.870
There might be something going on here.

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:18.730
Of course there is.

00:16:18.730 --> 00:16:22.410
For instance, if answering a 
question meant you would die,

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:24.270
would you answer it?

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:26.650
Who would die?

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:27.880
The person who answered?

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:30.300
For now, have some tea.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.060
I dunno the rules for 
proper tea drinking.

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:34.220
And if I did, I wouldn't care.

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:46.390
Anyway, if there was 
a question like that,

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.020
if I needed to, I'd ask the question,

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:50.360
and if I had to, I'd give
the answer, I guess.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.830
If you're that sure, then very well.

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:55.780
This is the place closest 
to the next world.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:57.460
If it's that close to the next world,

00:16:57.460 --> 00:16:59.440
one little thing could mean death.

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:02.000
Then if I'd made even a little mistake

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.370
on my way here, would I have died?

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:07.110
Of course, yes.

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:08.850
For example, if you'd tried to return

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:12.840
through the first door,
 you would've died for sure.

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:15.760
And if you couldn't answer the 
question, you would've died, too.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.390
Scary.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:22.480
But if life and death are 
nothing but an empty, eternal repetition,

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:25.940
then the one truth is that
you have no place to return to.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:29.400
If one side is death, 
then what is the other?

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:32.130
There's no point in 
asking that question.

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:33.170
Correct.

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:35.300
"Meaningless" is the correct answer.

00:17:35.300 --> 00:17:38.370
So then, do words have any meaning?

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:39.870
Not a clue.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:40.920
Correct.

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:43.500
"I cannot answer," 
is the correct answer.

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:46.720
If nothing else, you must believe

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:49.380
there is meaning in the meaningless, 
and continue to speak.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:53.710
I can't believe somebody who 
says there's nothing at all.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:55.290
Very true.

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:57.210
But you want something certain.

00:17:57.210 --> 00:17:59.290
And I do have one thing.

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:01.800
The war with wheat.

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:05.890
Wheat?

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:09.870
Do you mean that wheat is 
attacking the country of rice?

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:10.610
Yes.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.830
Nice and simple!

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:17.240
If we beat them, that means 
we can go back, right?

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:19.010
D-Do you think?

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:21.490
I'm not really sure...

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:23.910
Either way, first we kill, then we think.

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:27.110
That might be the kind of 
person you are, Boss, but...

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:30.040
There they are.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:31.780
That's the wheat?

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:33.300
Lots of 'em.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:34.430
Let's go!

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:04.620
What is this?

00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:10.450
They are awaiting the time.

00:19:10.450 --> 00:19:12.210
What? What time?

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:15.880
The time of destruction.

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:16.710
Destruction?

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:17.720
They're going to die?

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:21.080
Destruction and death are different.

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:26.260
They await the one destined to devour them.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:30.730
Before they die, they wish to be 
destroyed, to fulfill their task.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:34.870
And the person who does 
that is their savior.

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:37.290
What does that mean?

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:43.050
Devour them? Their task?

00:19:43.650 --> 00:19:44.950
No way...

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:03.630
First it bubbles, then it steams.

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:07.050
First it bubbles, then it steams.

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:11.060
When it's good and ready, 
put out the flame,

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:14.330
and even if the hungry baby 
cries, don't take the lid off!

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:18.190
Then take a little bit of straw,

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:24.660
and if it burns, you're all done.

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:26.140
Oh no!

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:29.130
If you don't eat them, the rice's 
existence will have no meaning.

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:30.520
Now, climb!

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:34.540
That means it's finally 
time to eat, right?

00:20:58.480 --> 00:20:59.990
This is really bad!

00:20:59.990 --> 00:21:03.110
If this isn't a dream, I'm dead!

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:08.450
It's hell down there, but in here...

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:11.740
it's heaven!

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:19.220
I'll never be able to eat all this!

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:23.930
So yummy!

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:27.720
So yummy!

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:30.060
I'm so glad you're awake!

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:32.630
What? What's going on?

00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:35.100
I think I was sleeping...

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:37.380
You just showed up here.

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:39.900
And you've got that nice 
kimono on. What happened?

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:42.380
I don't know what to tell you.

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:45.200
I was just dreaming.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.200
I went to this country 
with all this rice.

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:52.730
It wasn't a dream!

00:21:52.730 --> 00:21:53.980
What is this?

00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:55.290
Is it really rice?

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:56.940
It's real!

00:21:56.940 --> 00:21:58.110
Wow!

00:21:58.110 --> 00:22:00.150
All this rice keeps coming out!

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:02.880
Wow! You're like the god of rice!

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:05.840
Aww, I'm not a god.

00:22:06.460 --> 00:22:10.700
But now I can eat rice whenever I want!

00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:47.980
Hey, next time they say it's

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:49.770
Houjou Sou'un, the ambitious princess!

00:23:49.770 --> 00:23:51.620
Next time on Sengoku Collection:

00:23:51.620 --> 00:23:54.070
"Ambitious Princess Part 1!"

00:23:54.070 --> 00:23:56.930
Houjou can mean "great 
harvest" in Japanese!

00:23:56.930 --> 00:23:58.890
What a great name!
